# codex-skills/ is a markdown-only reference directory (no Python, no Node).
# This .gitignore is intentionally short — it just catches the things attendees
# or facilitators might accidentally generate while testing the skill inside
# this directory.

# --- operating system -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- editors / IDEs ---------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# --- secrets in case someone drops a .env in here while experimenting ------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Codex CLI local state --------------------------------------------------
# If a facilitator runs `codex` from inside this directory while demoing, it
# may create a project-scoped .codex/ hierarchy. The skill files themselves
# (spec-driven/, agents/, AGENTS.md.example) are tracked above; the state and
# per-project trust files below are not.
.codex/sessions/
.codex/log/
.codex/cache/
.codex/config.toml
